#. type: Content of: <sect1><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/kde/kf6/kf6-intro.xml:19
#, xml-text
msgid "KDE Frameworks 6 Pre-installation Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><indexterm><primary>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/kde/kf6/kf6-intro.xml:22
#, xml-text
msgid "KDE Frameworks Introduction"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/kde/kf6/kf6-intro.xml:26
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"KF6 can be installed in <filename class=\"directory\">/usr</filename> or "
"<filename class=\"directory\">/opt/kf6</filename>. The BLFS editors "
"recommend the latter in the BLFS environment."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/kde/kf6/kf6-intro.xml:32
#, xml-text
msgid "Installing in /usr"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/kde/kf6/kf6-intro.xml:35
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"One option is to install <application>KDE Frameworks</application> into the "
"<filename class=\"directory\">/usr</filename> hierarchy.  This creates a "
"simpler setup but makes it more difficult to try multiple versions of "
"<application>KDE Frameworks</application>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/kde/kf6/kf6-intro.xml:41
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>export KF6_PREFIX=/usr</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/kde/kf6/kf6-intro.xml:44
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"It is a good idea to add the following variables to your system or personal "
"profiles:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/kde/kf6/kf6-intro.xml:48
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt;&gt; /etc/profile.d/qt6.sh &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin kf6 extension for /etc/profile.d/qt6.sh\n"
"\n"
"pathappend /usr/lib/plugins        QT_PLUGIN_PATH\n"
"pathappend $QT6DIR/lib/plugins     QT_PLUGIN_PATH\n"
"\n"
"pathappend /usr/lib/qt6/qml        QML2_IMPORT_PATH\n"
"pathappend $QT6DIR/lib/qml         QML2_IMPORT_PATH\n"
"\n"
"# End extension for /etc/profile.d/qt6.sh</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"\n"
"cat &gt; /etc/profile.d/kf6.sh &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin /etc/profile.d/kf6.sh\n"
"\n"
"export KF6_PREFIX=/usr\n"
"\n"
"# End /etc/profile.d/kf6.sh</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/kde/kf6/kf6-intro.xml:70
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If <application>qt6</application> was installed in <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/usr</filename>, the <filename "
"class=\"directory\">$QT6DIR/lib/</filename> portions of the above paths may "
"need to be changed to <filename "
"class=\"directory\">$QT6DIR/lib/qt6/</filename>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/kde/kf6/kf6-intro.xml:79
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Additionally, if <xref linkend=\"sudo\"/> is installed, these variables "
"should be available to the super user. Execute the following commands as the"
" <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/kde/kf6/kf6-intro.xml:84
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt;&gt; /etc/sudoers.d/qt &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal>Defaults env_keep += QT_PLUGIN_PATH\n"
"Defaults env_keep += QML2_IMPORT_PATH</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"\n"
"cat &gt;&gt; /etc/sudoers.d/kde &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal>Defaults env_keep += KF6_PREFIX</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/kde/kf6/kf6-intro.xml:96
#, xml-text
msgid "Installing in /opt"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/kde/kf6/kf6-intro.xml:99
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"A method of building multiple versions installs <application>KDE "
"Frameworks</application> in the <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/opt</filename> hierarchy:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/kde/kf6/kf6-intro.xml:104
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>export KF6_PREFIX=/opt/kf6</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/kde/kf6/kf6-intro.xml:107
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you are not installing <application>KDE Frameworks</application> in "
"<filename class=\"directory\">/usr</filename>, you will need to make some "
"additional configuration changes. Best practice is to add those to your "
"system or personal profile:"
msgstr ""

#.  Don't set MANPATH, see why on the bash startup files page
#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/kde/kf6/kf6-intro.xml:113
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt; /etc/profile.d/kf6.sh &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin /etc/profile.d/kf6.sh\n"
"\n"
"export KF6_PREFIX=/opt/kf6\n"
"\n"
"pathappend $KF6_PREFIX/bin              PATH\n"
"pathappend $KF6_PREFIX/lib/pkgconfig    PKG_CONFIG_PATH\n"
"\n"
"pathappend $KF6_PREFIX/etc/xdg          XDG_CONFIG_DIRS\n"
"pathappend $KF6_PREFIX/share            XDG_DATA_DIRS\n"
"\n"
"pathappend $KF6_PREFIX/lib/plugins      QT_PLUGIN_PATH\n"
"pathappend $KF6_PREFIX/lib/plugins/kcms QT_PLUGIN_PATH\n"
"\n"
"pathappend $KF6_PREFIX/lib/qml          QML2_IMPORT_PATH\n"
"\n"
"pathappend $KF6_PREFIX/lib/python&python3-majorver;/site-packages PYTHONPATH\n"
"\n"
"pathappend $KF6_PREFIX/include          CPLUS_INCLUDE_PATH\n"
"\n"
"pathappend $KF6_PREFIX/lib/gtk-3.0      GTK_PATH\n"
"# End /etc/profile.d/kf6.sh</literal>\n"
"EOF\n"
"\n"
"cat &gt;&gt; /etc/profile.d/qt6.sh &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin Qt6 changes for KF6\n"
"\n"
"pathappend /usr/lib/plugins            QT_PLUGIN_PATH\n"
"pathappend $QT6DIR/plugins             QT_PLUGIN_PATH\n"
"pathappend $QT6DIR/qml                 QML2_IMPORT_PATH\n"
"\n"
"# End Qt6 changes for KF6</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/kde/kf6/kf6-intro.xml:148
#, xml-text
msgid "Expand your <filename>/etc/ld.so.conf</filename> file:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/kde/kf6/kf6-intro.xml:151
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt;&gt; /etc/ld.so.conf &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin KF6 addition\n"
"\n"
"/opt/kf6/lib\n"
"\n"
"# End KF6 addition</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><indexterm><primary>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/kde/kf6/kf6-intro.xml:160
#, xml-text
msgid "/etc/ld.so.conf"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/kde/kf6/kf6-intro.xml:164
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Several <application>KDE Frameworks</application> and "
"<application>Plasma</application> packages install files into "
"<application>D-Bus</application> and <application>Polkit</application> "
"directories. When installing <application>KDE Frameworks</application> in a "
"location other than <filename class=\"directory\">/usr</filename>, "
"<application>D-Bus</application> and <application>Polkit</application> need "
"to be able to find these files.  The easiest way to achieve this is to "
"create the following symlinks (as the <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/kde/kf6/kf6-intro.xml:177
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>install -v -dm755           $KF6_PREFIX/{etc,share} &amp;&amp;\n"
"ln -sfv /etc/dbus-1         $KF6_PREFIX/etc         &amp;&amp;\n"
"ln -sfv /usr/share/dbus-1   $KF6_PREFIX/share       &amp;&amp;\n"
"ln -sfv /usr/share/polkit-1 $KF6_PREFIX/share</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/kde/kf6/kf6-intro.xml:183
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Several <application>KDE Frameworks</application> and <application>KDE "
"Plasma</application> packages install files into "
"<application>D-Bus</application>, <application>Polkit</application>, and "
"<application>systemd</application> directories. When installing "
"<application>KDE 6</application> in a location other than <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/usr</filename>, <application>D-Bus</application>, "
"<application>Polkit</application>, and <application>systemd</application> "
"need to be able to find these files.  The easiest way to achieve this is to "
"create the following symlinks (as the <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/kde/kf6/kf6-intro.xml:198
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>install -v -dm755           $KF6_PREFIX/{etc,share} &amp;&amp;\n"
"ln -sfv /etc/dbus-1         $KF6_PREFIX/etc         &amp;&amp;\n"
"ln -sfv /usr/share/dbus-1   $KF6_PREFIX/share       &amp;&amp;\n"
"ln -sfv /usr/share/polkit-1 $KF6_PREFIX/share       &amp;&amp;\n"
"install -v -dm755           $KF6_PREFIX/lib         &amp;&amp;\n"
"ln -sfv /usr/lib/systemd    $KF6_PREFIX/lib</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/kde/kf6/kf6-intro.xml:206
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Some packages may also install icons from the \"hicolor\" icon set. Since "
"that icon set is used by many packages, it is a good idea to create a "
"symlink to the one in <filename class=\"directory\">/usr/share</filename> to"
" avoid having multiple installations of <xref linkend=\"hicolor-icon-"
"theme\"/>.  Run the following commands as the <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/kde/kf6/kf6-intro.xml:214
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>install -v -dm755                $KF6_PREFIX/share/icons &amp;&amp;\n"
"ln -sfv /usr/share/icons/hicolor $KF6_PREFIX/share/icons</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><tip><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/kde/kf6/kf6-intro.xml:219
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Sometimes, the installation paths are hardcoded into installed files.  This "
"is the reason why <filename class=\"directory\">/opt/kf6</filename> is used "
"as installation prefix instead of <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/opt/kf6-&kf6-version;</filename>. After installing "
"<application>KDE Frameworks</application>, you may rename the directory and "
"create a symlink:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><tip><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/kde/kf6/kf6-intro.xml:227
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>mv /opt/kf6{,-&kf6-version;}\n"
"ln -sfv kf6-&kf6-version; /opt/kf6</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><tip><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/kde/kf6/kf6-intro.xml:231
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Later on, you may want to install other versions of <application>KDE "
"Frameworks</application>. To do that, just remove the symlink and use "
"<filename class=\"directory\">/opt/kf6</filename> as the prefix again. Which"
" version of <application>KDE Frameworks</application> you use depends only "
"on where the symlink points. No other reconfiguration will be needed."
msgstr ""
